{"format":"portfolio-builder/project","version":1,"name":"Hayoon Jung — Frontend Engineer","savedAt":"2026-11-13T11:13:14.365Z","doc":{"current":"p15a","theme":"cloud","typeset":"geist","global":{"radius":8,"gap":24,"padding":0,"marginX":0,"maxWidth":1240,"border":0,"gridGuide":false,"gridCols":12},"site":{"navMode":"anchor","navSync":true,"title":"Hayoon Jung — Frontend Engineer","description":"Frontend engineer with five years on design systems, performance and accessibility. Four selected projects, each with the number that mattered.","favLetter":"H","favColor":"#111111","lang":"en","ogImage":null,"siteUrl":"","background":{"kind":"none","image":null,"video":null,"poster":null,"mode":"고정","dim":0.35,"blur":0,"gray":0,"gradient":false,"scrollFx":"없음","grain":0},"enterFx":"아래에서 올라오기","enterDelay":2,"scrollBar":true,"smoothScroll":true,"cursor":false,"snapScroll":false,"introLoader":false,"headFixed1":true},"pages":[{"id":"p15a","name":"Home","wireframe":"sticky-split","fills":{"b":"aside","c":"section","d":"section","x1-1":"gallery","x3-1":"footer","xw-1":"links","xw-2":"bcard"},"extra":[{"id":"x1","cols":1,"at":2},{"id":"xw","cols":2,"at":2},{"id":"x3","cols":1,"at":2}],"content":{"b":{"photo":{"id":"imgp15mark","alt":"HJ monogram","fit":"cover","w":700,"h":700,"bytes":23178},"photoSize":86,"photoRound":false,"name":"Hayoon Jung","role":"Frontend Engineer","bio":"I build interfaces that stay fast and usable as teams grow.\n\nCurrently in Seoul, working remotely with a team in Berlin.","showMenu":true,"linkTo":"이 페이지 섹션","sticky":true,"align":"start"},"c":{"title":"About","body":"For five years I have worked on keeping large frontends consistent while many people change them at the same time.\n\nThat work took me through design systems, performance and accessibility. In each case the approach was similar: write the rule down once and make it easy for every team to follow.\n\nBefore engineering I studied industrial design, so I still sketch a feature before I build it. Outside work I go climbing and read about typography.","columns":1,"align":"start","listStyle":"none","items":[]},"d":{"title":"Experience","body":"","columns":1,"align":"start","listStyle":"timeline","items":[{"label":"2024 – present","note":"Senior Frontend Engineer at Loomstack (design system, checkout, hiring)"},{"label":"2022 – 2024","note":"Frontend Engineer at Northbay (Angular to React migration across 38 routes)"},{"label":"2021 – 2022","note":"Frontend Engineer at Ordinal Labs (first hire on the web team)"},{"label":"2020 – 2021","note":"Product Designer, then engineer, at Studio Pale (built the first React app)"}]},"x1-1":{"title":"Selected Work","columns":2,"rows":0,"ratio":0.72,"showThumb":true,"grayHover":false,"items":[{"image":{"id":"imgp15w1","alt":"Design system component library","fit":"cover","w":1600,"h":1102,"bytes":53781},"title":"Design System","stack":"React · TypeScript · Storybook","desc":"One library adopted by 40+ products","detail":"The problem: six teams had six button components. None of them agreed on focus states, and two were inaccessible.\n\nWhat I did: built a single library with tokens for colour, spacing and motion, then wrote a codemod so teams could migrate a screen in an afternoon rather than a sprint.\n\nThe number that mattered: adoption. 40+ products on the library within a year, because migrating was cheaper than not migrating.","link":"https://github.com/","status":"운영중"},{"image":{"id":"imgp15w2","alt":"Checkout performance before and after","fit":"cover","w":1600,"h":1102,"bytes":49554},"title":"Checkout Performance","stack":"Next.js · Web Vitals · Lighthouse CI","desc":"LCP 4.1s → 1.6s on mid-tier Android","detail":"The problem: checkout was fast on our laptops but very slow on the phones most of our customers used.\n\nWhat I did: measured on a real mid-tier Android instead of a throttled desktop, then went after the three biggest costs: route-level code splitting, an image CDN with AVIF, and deferring third-party tags that nobody owned.\n\nThe number that mattered: 4.1s to 1.6s LCP, and a Lighthouse CI budget in the pipeline so it stays there. Conversion also went up.","link":"https://github.com/","status":"완료"},{"image":{"id":"imgp15w3","alt":"Accessibility contrast and focus order","fit":"cover","w":1600,"h":1102,"bytes":63578},"title":"Accessibility Pass","stack":"axe-core · Playwright · VoiceOver","desc":"312 issues closed, 0 critical remaining","detail":"The problem: an audit came back with 312 findings and the team had no idea where to start.\n\nWhat I did: sorted by \"how many screens does this touch\", fixed the shared components first, and added axe-core to the component test suite so the same class of bug could not come back.\n\nThe number that mattered: zero critical issues twelve months later. The test suite now catches them before review.","link":"https://github.com/","status":"완료"},{"image":{"id":"imgp15w4","alt":"Incremental migration timeline","fit":"cover","w":1600,"h":1102,"bytes":75757},"title":"Incremental Migration","stack":"React · Module Federation · Playwright","desc":"Angular 9 → React, zero downtime, 14 months","detail":"The problem: a full rewrite had been proposed twice and rejected both times, because the application could not stop shipping for a year.\n\nWhat I did: put a React shell around the existing router so both frameworks could run behind one URL space, shared the design tokens as a plain CSS layer, then moved two routes per sprint.\n\nThe number that mattered: zero downtime across 38 routes, and a 41% smaller bundle once the old shell came out. It took longer than a rewrite would have on paper, but it was finished.","link":"https://github.com/","status":"진행중"}],"stackStyle":"배지","phone2":true,"tagFilter":true},"x3-1":{"text":"© 2026 Hayoon Jung","email":"hayoon@example.com","showMenu":false,"align":"space-between","showTime":true,"timeCity":"Seoul","timeZone":"Asia/Seoul","footStyle":"표준","bizName":"Hayoon Jung","ceo":"","bizNo":"","address":"","tel":"","mailOrder":"","regNo":"","privacyUrl":""},"xw-1":{"title":"Writing","style":"text","align":"start","newTab":true,"items":[{"label":"A design system is a migration problem","url":"https://example.com/","desc":"","file":null},{"label":"Measure on the device your users actually hold","url":"https://example.com/","desc":"","file":null},{"label":"Accessibility is a test suite, not a checklist","url":"https://example.com/","desc":"","file":null},{"label":"Why our rewrite proposals kept getting rejected","url":"https://example.com/","desc":"","file":null}]},"xw-2":{"faces":"앞·뒤 (누르면 뒤집기)","paper":45,"design":"스위스","role":"Frontend","roleSub":"Engineer","name":"Hayoon Jung","nameEn":"정하윤","title":"Frontend Engineer","org":"","phone":"","email":"","location":"Seoul, KR","site":"","label":"PORTFOLIO 2026","initials":"HJ","tagline":"Fewer things, done properly.","stack":"TypeScript · React · Design Systems","accent":"","iconStyle":"윤곽 원형","qr":true,"qrPos":"자동","vcf":true,"width":460}},"overrides":{"b":{"padding":48,"minHeight":520,"border":0,"typo":{"fs":15,"leading":1.65,"muted":"#5b6270"}},"c":{"padding":48,"minHeight":520,"border":0,"typo":{"fs":16,"leading":1.75,"muted":"#5b6270"}},"d":{"padding":48,"border":0,"typo":{"fs":15,"leading":1.7,"muted":"#5b6270"}},"x1-1":{"padding":48,"border":0,"typo":{"muted":"#5b6270"}},"x2-1":{"padding":48,"border":0,"bg":"#fafafa","typo":{"muted":"#5b6270"}},"x3-1":{"padding":40,"border":0,"typo":{"fs":14,"muted":"#5b6270"}},"xw-1":{"minHeight":260},"xw-2":{"minHeight":260}},"fx":{"c":[{"name":"reveal","options":{"preset":"rise","duration":700,"distance":18}}],"d":[{"name":"reveal","options":{"preset":"rise","duration":700,"distance":18}}],"x1-1":[{"name":"reveal","options":{"preset":"rise","duration":760,"distance":22}}],"xw-1":[{"name":"reveal","options":{"preset":"rise","duration":700,"distance":18}}],"xw-2":[{"name":"tilt","options":{"maxTilt":8,"perspective":900,"scale":1.02,"speed":400,"glare":true,"maxGlare":0.18,"axis":"both"}}]}}]},"assets":{"imgp15mark":"data:image/png;base64,","imgp15w1":"data:image/png;base64,","imgp15w2":"data:image/png;base64,","imgp15w3":"data:image/png;base64,","imgp15w4":"data:image/png;base64,"}}